[ENTITY stark:1534594 | Exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential under the influence of the generalized uncertainty principle]
[TEXT]
{"canonical_id":"stark:1534594","content":null,"evidence_id":"text:paper:1534594:overlay","overlay":{"origin":"phase4_evaluation_overlay","overlay_sha256":"ce96bbd1f2e6e1771c090b8c6c9f2db6b6d50f3a42a9aa9ce4f7dfa5877818da"},"payload":{"abstract":"We present an effective method of exact solution of the (1+1)-dimensional Dirac equation with a linear scalar-like potential in the context of the generalized uncertainty principle (GUP). The effectiveness of the method depends on knowledge of the energy spectrum of the harmonic oscillator with GUP. We employ the property of the harmonic oscillator that the kinetic energy part of the Hamiltonian is of equal weight to the potential energy part to obtain the energy levels from the deformation of the Dirac equation with a scalar-like linear potential through the generalized Heisenberg algebra of a GUP. Our result fully coincides with the results found in the literature. This paper thus provides an easier, alternative and effective method of exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential with GUP.","content":"Exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential under the influence of the generalized uncertainty principle\n\nWe present an effective method of exact solution of the (1+1)-dimensional Dirac equation with a linear scalar-like potential in the context of the generalized uncertainty principle (GUP). The effectiveness of the method depends on knowledge of the energy spectrum of the harmonic oscillator with GUP. We employ the property of the harmonic oscillator that the kinetic energy part of the Hamiltonian is of equal weight to the potential energy part to obtain the energy levels from the deformation of the Dirac equation with a scalar-like linear potential through the generalized Heisenberg algebra of a GUP. Our result fully coincides with the results found in the literature. This paper thus provides an easier, alternative and effective method of exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential with GUP.","evaluation_overlay":true,"paper_id":1534594,"title":"Exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential under the influence of the generalized uncertainty principle"},"source":"text"}
