[ENTITY stark:1606518 | Minimal length Dirac equation revisited]
[TEXT]
{"canonical_id":"stark:1606518","content":null,"evidence_id":"text:paper:1606518:overlay","overlay":{"origin":"phase4_evaluation_overlay","overlay_sha256":"ce96bbd1f2e6e1771c090b8c6c9f2db6b6d50f3a42a9aa9ce4f7dfa5877818da"},"payload":{"abstract":"We will show that the Dirac equation under the assumption of a generalized uncertainty principle corresponds to a Schrodinger-like equation with a new effective potential. Next, as typical examples, the potential well and the step potential are studied in an exact analytical manner. The scattering problems as well as the reflection and transmission parameters are reported.","content":"Minimal length Dirac equation revisited\n\nWe will show that the Dirac equation under the assumption of a generalized uncertainty principle corresponds to a Schrodinger-like equation with a new effective potential. Next, as typical examples, the potential well and the step potential are studied in an exact analytical manner. The scattering problems as well as the reflection and transmission parameters are reported.","evaluation_overlay":true,"paper_id":1606518,"title":"Minimal length Dirac equation revisited"},"source":"text"}
